      "en": "Sweden's northernmost weather radar stands on high ground outside Kiruna, about 640 m above sea level and well north of the Arctic Circle, watching the mountains and valleys of Swedish Lapland. Modernised on its existing site, it was the last of SMHI's twelve radars to return, in February 2021; the site dates from 1996."
